[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Jeff decides to play with a Magic 8 Ball. Each time he asks it a question, it has a 2/5 chance of giving him a positive answer. If he asks it 5 questions, what is the probability that it gives him exactly 2 positive answers?
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m To solve this problem, we can use the binomial probability formula. The binomial probability formula is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = k) = \binom{n}{k} p^k (1-p)^{n-k} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m where:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m - \( n \) is the number of trials (in this case, 5 questions),
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m - \( k \) is the number of successes (in this case, 2 positive answers),
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m - \( p \) is the probability of success on an individual trial (in this case, \( \frac{2}{5} \)),
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m - \( \binom{n}{k} \) is the binomial coefficient, which is calculated as \( \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \).
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Plugging in the values, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = 2) = \binom{5}{2} \left( \frac{2}{5} \right)^2 \left( 1 - \frac{2}{5} \right)^{5-2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m First, calculate the binomial coefficient:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \binom{5}{2} = \frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \frac{5!}{2!3!} = \frac{5 \times 4 \times 3!}{2 \times 1 \times 3!} = \frac{5 \times 4}{2 \times 1} = 10 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Next, calculate \( \left( \frac{2}{5} \right)^2 \):
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \left( \frac{2}{5} \right)^2 = \frac{2^2}{5^2} = \frac{4}{25} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Then, calculate \( \left( 1 - \frac{2}{5} \right)^{5-2} \):
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ 1 - \frac{2}{5} = \frac{5}{5} - \frac{2}{5} = \frac{3}{5} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \left( \frac{3}{5} \right)^3 = \frac{3^3}{5^3} = \frac{27}{125} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Now, combine these results:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = 2) = 10 \times \frac{4}{25} \times \frac{27}{125} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = 2) = 10 \times \frac{4 \times 27}{25 \times 125} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = 2) = 10 \times \frac{108}{3125} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ P(X = 2) = \frac{1080}{3125} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \boxed{\frac{1080}{3125}} \]<|im_end|>
