[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m To determine the largest value of \( k \) for which both \( Q_1(x) = x^2 + (k - 29)x - k \) and \( Q_2(x) = 2x^2 + (2k - 43)x + k \) can be factors of a cubic polynomial \( P(x) \), we need to consider the roots of \( P(x) \). If \( Q_1(x) \) and \( Q_2(x) \) are factors of \( P(x) \), then \( P(x) \) must have roots that are the reciprocals of the roots of \( Q_1(x) \) and \( Q_2(x) \) respectively. This means that the roots of \( P(x) \) must be the reciprocals of the roots of \( Q_1(x) \) and \( Q_2(x) \), and vice versa. Therefore, the pairs of roots of \( P(x) \) must be \(\left( \frac{k-29}{2}, \frac{k}{2} \right)\) and \(\left( \frac{2k-43}{k}, \frac{1}{k} \right)\).
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m There are two conditions for the roots of \( P(x) \). The first condition is that the product of the roots must equal the constant term for both \( Q_1(x) \) and \( Q_2(x) \), and the second condition is that the sum of the roots must equal the coefficient of \( x \) for both \( Q_1(x) \) and \( Q_2(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Setting the product of the roots equal to the constant term for both polynomials, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \left( \frac{k-29}{2} \right) \left( \frac{k}{2} \right) = k \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ \frac{k^2 - 29k}{4} = k \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ k^2 - 29k = 4k \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[ k^2 - 33k = 0 \]
