[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m First, observe that the third congruence \( x \equiv 10 \pmod{13} \) can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m x = 13k + 10 \quad \text{for some integer } k.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Next, substitute \( x = 13k + 10 \) into the first congruence \( x \equiv 5 \pmod{7} \):
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 13k + 10 \equiv 5 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Simplify \( 13 \pmod{7} \):
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 13 \equiv 6 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Thus, the congruence becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 6k + 10 \equiv 5 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Subtract 10 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 6k \equiv -5 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Since \(-5 \equiv 2 \pmod{7}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 6k \equiv 2 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m To solve for \( k \), we need the multiplicative inverse of 6 modulo 7. The inverse of 6 modulo 7 is a number \( y \) such that:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 6y \equiv 1 \pmod{7}.
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m By testing values, we find:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
