[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m We can solve these equations step by step. First, we can express \( n \) in terms of \( c \) and \( i \) from the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m n = 80 - c - i
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m Next, we substitute \( n \) from the first equation into the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 5c - 2i = 232
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 5c - 2i = 232
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m We can solve for \( i \) in terms of \( c \):
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m 2i = 5c - 232
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3407)[0m i = \frac{5c - 232}{2}
